course: dictionary
lesson: 8037
title: Words that come back to life
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Look at the words around the word and ask: what is happening here? «Bots also add a little randomness, so pressing "regenerate" gives a new story.» Pressing it makes a new story, so regenerate means to make something again, fresh and new.
explain: Regenerate has a science meaning too. A lizard can regenerate a tail, which means it grows a new one after losing the old one. A starfish can regenerate an arm. In both cases the word means to grow again after being damaged or lost.
explain: Context can also show you when the word is about a place. «Regenerate the town centre» means bringing new life, jobs and activity to a run-down town. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you are probably right.
fact: Regenerate means to grow again after being damaged or lost, or to make something new or fresh again.
fact: A lizard can regenerate a tail, and a starfish can regenerate an arm.
fact: A burnt forest can regenerate, which means new trees grow back over time.
fact: On a computer, to regenerate a page or a password means to make it again.
fact: Use the words around the word to choose the right meaning, then check by putting your meaning into the sentence.
exercise: In the sentence «pressing "regenerate" gives a new story», what does pressing regenerate make? | *A new story | A copy of the same old story | A picture of a bot | A broken button
exercise: «A starfish can regenerate an arm.» What does this mean? | *It grows a new arm after losing one | It throws its arms away | It paints its arms bright colours | It hides its arms in the sand
exercise: «The council wants to regenerate the run-down town centre.» What does regenerate mean here? | *Bring new life, jobs and activity back | Make the town centre smaller | Move the whole town to the coast | Knock the buildings down and leave a hole
test: Trees in a burnt forest can regenerate over time. What does regenerate mean? | Catch fire again | *Grow again after being damaged | Fall down and rot away | Move to a new place
test: On a computer, you can regenerate a password. Which meaning fits best? | Share it with your friends | Print it out | *Make it again | Lose it for ever
exam: Which words in «Bots also add a little randomness, so pressing "regenerate" gives a new story» show what regenerate does? | Bots also add | The same question | Two bots can | *Gives a new story
